(Bug #95. `Set NAME to VALUE.` on a name that does not exist yet brings it
 into being with the value's type (LANGUAGE.md "Two Canonical Forms"). The
 text and the map are the two that had no type at all: the slot was read by
 the integer formatter, so this file printed the string's ADDRESS and the
 map's struct pointer instead of what was put in them.)

Set tally to 5.
Print tally.

Set ratio to 2.5.
Print ratio.

Set label to "hello".
Print label.

Set ready to true.
Print ready.

Set colours to ["red", "green"].
Print colours.

Set ages to {"ann": 30}.
Print ages.
